macOS: swap %gs:0x20 between Tib.FiberData and the pthread QoS slot at every crossing.

Patch 0008 mirrors Tib.FiberData into %gs:0x20 so that GetCurrentFiber(), a
compiler intrinsic that reads that slot directly, returns the real fiber. It
documented the cost: on macOS that slot is the thread's pthread QoS class, read
by libdispatch and pthread, and the mirror clobbers it for any thread that uses
fibers.

MEASURED (M1 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, 2026-09-12, Metaphor: ReFantazio Prologue Demo,
Steam 3130330):

  * On the engine without 0008 (Sikarugir Wine 10, r0 to r2) the game faults
    seconds after launch reading 0x20FF, the QoS value for the thread it just
    created fibers on, right after CreateFiber and SwitchToFiber in the relay
    trace. Same with AVX advertised and on DXVK, so only the fiber slot is
    involved. This is the Guardians of the Galaxy defect 0008 fixes.
  * On the engine with 0008 (Wine 11, r5 to r7) the game gets a window, then
    the process hangs at full CPU with the window black. A `sample` of the
    process shows the Cocoa main thread inside Wine's signal handler after a
    fault in libdispatch's _dispatch_set_priority_and_voucher_slow, and three
    worker threads more than a thousand frames deep in nested exception
    dispatch. The game's job threads switch fibers and also drive winemac.drv,
    so blocks reach the main queue carrying a fiber pointer where libdispatch
    expects a priority, and the main queue faults on it. Guardians never takes
    that path.

Windows and macOS both fix the offset, so the two values cannot share the slot;
they can take turns. This patch gives the slot to whichever side is running:

  * signal_init_thread keeps the host QoS value in a new
    amd64_thread_data field (host_qos, TEB+0x340) before anything else runs.
  * Every entry into unix code writes host_qos back into %gs:0x20: the syscall
    dispatcher, the unix-call dispatcher, and user_mode_callback_return.
  * Every return to PE code writes Tib.FiberData into %gs:0x20:
    __wine_syscall_dispatcher_return (which also covers thread start, APC and
    exception delivery, since they all leave through it), the unix-call
    dispatcher's own fast return (it does not pass through the label above
    unless restore_flags is set), and call_user_mode_callback (window
    procedures and other callbacks).

Register choice matters in the unix-call dispatcher: its fast return restores
only %r13, %rsi and %rdi and relies on the SysV callee-saved registers for the
rest, so the swap there uses %rax on entry (dead until the call) and %rdx on
return (volatile for the PE caller). The first build of this patch used %r15
on entry and every process died at the first unix call after it, in
build_module, reading through the clobbered %r15 (measured, 2026-09-12).
  * The three kernelbase sites from 0008 keep writing the slot while PE code
    owns it; TEB->Tib.FiberData stays the source of truth.

Threads that never run PE code (the Cocoa main thread, libdispatch workers)
keep their QoS value untouched, because nothing writes the slot on them any
more: 0008 never wrote it at thread start, and this patch only reads it there.

COST: two moves per crossing on macOS, none elsewhere. Unix code running inside
a signal handler on a PE thread still sees the fiber pointer in the slot; Wine's
handlers do not call libdispatch, so this is accepted.

NOT VERIFIED at the time of writing: that Metaphor plays with this patch, and
that Guardians still does. Both are the tests for the engine built from it.

UPSTREAM: nothing to send, and the earlier sentence here claiming upstream Wine
has the same conflict was wrong. Upstream solved the whole class in Wine 10.5
(Brendan Shanks, 3a16aabbf5, "ntdll: On macOS x86_64, swap GSBASE between the
TEB and macOS TSD when entering/leaving PE code"): the dispatchers switch the
entire gs base with the private _thread_set_tsd_base syscall, so PE code sees
the real TEB (including Tib.FiberData at 0x20) and unix code sees the pthread
block. Wine 10.0 to 10.4 and the CrossOver 26.3 source tree this engine is
built from do not carry that change (measured: zero references in either).
This patch is the one-slot alternative for such trees, two moves per crossing
instead of a syscall. The better long-term fix for this engine is to backport
the upstream gs base switch.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c	2026-09-12 19:10:21
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c	2026-09-12 19:37:50
@@ -508,11 +508,13 @@
     void                **instrumentation_callback; /* 0330 */
     DWORD                 fs;            /* 0338 WOW TEB selector */
     DWORD                 mxcsr;         /* 033c Unix-side mxcsr register */
+    DWORD_PTR             host_qos;      /* 0340 macOS: the pthread QoS slot value, %gs:0x20, while PE code owns that slot */
 };
 
 C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct amd64_thread_data) <= sizeof(((struct ntdll_thread_data *)0)->cpu_data) );
 C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, pthread_teb ) == 0x320 );
 C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, frame_size ) == 0x328 );
+C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, host_qos ) == 0x340 );
 C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, instrumentation_callback ) == 0x330 );
 C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, fs ) == 0x338 );
 C_ASSERT( offsetof( TEB, GdiTebBatch ) + offsetof( struct amd64_thread_data, mxcsr ) == 0x33c );
@@ -1825,6 +1827,10 @@
                    "jz 1f\n\t"
                    "xchgq %rcx,%r10\n"
                    "1:\n\t"
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+                   "movq 0x20(%r13),%rax\n\t"      /* teb->Tib.FiberData: PE code owns %gs:0x20 from here */
+                   "movq %rax,%gs:0x20\n\t"
+#endif
                    "xor %rbx,%rbx\n\t"
                    "xor %r12,%r12\n\t"
                    "xor %r13,%r13\n\t"
@@ -1839,6 +1845,10 @@
 extern void DECLSPEC_NORETURN user_mode_callback_return( void *ret_ptr, ULONG ret_len,
                                                          NTSTATUS status, TEB *teb );
 __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( user_mode_callback_return,
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+                   "movq 0x340(%rcx),%r10\n\t" /* amd64_thread_data()->host_qos: unix code owns %gs:0x20 again */
+                   "movq %r10,%gs:0x20\n\t"
+#endif
                    "movq 0x378(%rcx),%r10\n\t" /* thread_data->syscall_frame */
                    "movq 0xa0(%r10),%r11\n\t"  /* frame->prev_frame */
                    "movq %r11,0x378(%rcx)\n\t" /* syscall_frame = prev_frame */
@@ -3076,6 +3086,12 @@
     __asm__ volatile ("movq %0,%%gs:%c1" :: "r" (teb->Tib.Self), "n" (FIELD_OFFSET(TEB, Tib.Self)));
     __asm__ volatile ("movq %0,%%gs:%c1" :: "r" (teb->ThreadLocalStoragePointer), "n" (FIELD_OFFSET(TEB, ThreadLocalStoragePointer)));
     __asm__ volatile ("movq %0,%%gs:%c1" :: "r" (teb->Peb), "n" (FIELD_OFFSET(TEB, Peb)));
+    /* %gs:0x20 is where PE code reads Tib.FiberData (GetCurrentFiber() is an intrinsic), and on
+     * macOS it is the pthread QoS class slot that libdispatch and pthread read. Both cannot hold
+     * the slot at once, so it is swapped at every crossing: unix code gets the host value back
+     * on entry (the dispatchers, user_mode_callback_return), PE code gets Tib.FiberData on
+     * return (__wine_syscall_dispatcher_return, call_user_mode_callback). Keep the host value. */
+    __asm__ volatile ("movq %%gs:%c1,%0" : "=r" (thread_data->host_qos) : "n" (FIELD_OFFSET(TEB, Tib.FiberData)));
     thread_data->pthread_teb = mac_thread_gsbase();
     /* alloc_tls_slot() needs to poke a value to an address relative to each
        thread's gsbase.  Have each thread record its gsbase pointer into its
@@ -3227,6 +3243,10 @@
                    __ASM_CFI_REG_IS_AT2(rbp, rcx, 0x98, 0x01)
                    "movq %gs:0x30,%r13\n\t"        /* teb */
                    "movl %eax,0xb0(%rcx)\n\t"      /* frame->syscall_id */
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+                   "movq 0x340(%r13),%r15\n\t"     /* amd64_thread_data()->host_qos */
+                   "movq %r15,%gs:0x20\n\t"        /* unix code sees the pthread QoS slot again */
+#endif
                    /* Legends of Runeterra hooks the first system call return instruction, and
                     * depends on us returning to it. Adjust the return address accordingly. */
                    "subq $0xb,0x70(%rcx)\n\t"
@@ -3335,6 +3355,11 @@
                    __ASM_CFI(".cfi_remember_state\n\t")
                    __ASM_CFI_CFA_IS_AT2(rcx, 0xa8, 0x01) /* frame->syscall_cfa */
                    "leaq 0x70(%rcx),%rsp\n\t"      /* %rsp > frame means no longer inside syscall */
+#ifdef __APPLE__
